Z||000002||mshill||12-17-2000||12:20 PM||||That's exatly what I used.  Two dolly's side by side with a 2x4 across the back and one across the front.  Fits perfectly and rolls OK.||||reg||14
Z||000003||Eric_PA||12-17-2000||01:14 PM||||I used a triangular setup. two sides where 50 inches and the side towards the back I made 45 inches. It worked great. It was made up of 2x4's and reinforced in the corners with 1/2 inch ply. Bolted heavu duty dolly type wheels from the hardware store in each corner. why use 4 wheels when you can get away with three.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cart.jpg"> <P>Eric<BR>Black 86.5 Ratmatic Fastback<BR>Red 84 4 speed<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000004||JohnnyK||12-17-2000||01:56 PM||||I just used two average (yet different) dolly's. One was a carpeted furniture dolly, and one was a homemade metal thing with plywood. Doesn't really matter.||||reg||1
